Stack navigation. stackNav turns the children of an element into a navigation stack. A new page slides in while the one below drifts back, and the top page can be swiped away from the left edge: it follows the finger and lands where the throw would carry it. Elements with the same data-shared value on two pages fly from one place to the other, with their size, on the way in and on the way back. Only the top page can be reached, focus moves to the new page and returns to the opener, a live region announces the title, and Alt+ArrowLeft goes back.
const nav = stackNav(document.querySelector("#app")); await nav.push(detailPage); await nav.pop();
A referee for gestures. A carousel inside a drawer, a sheet around a carousel and the swipe back at the edge all want the same finger. In 2.0 they decide: nothing moves until the finger has moved a few pixels, the direction picks the candidates, and the first part that can move that way wins. A carousel on its last slide declines, so the drawer around it takes the swipe. The same function, contend, is available for your own parts.

import { sheet, swipeStack } from "@weber-development/lagrangian-pro";
const filters = sheet(element, { detents: [0.4, 1], backdrop: shade }); openButton.onclick = () => filters.open();
const stack = swipeStack(cards, { onSwipe: (card, direction) => save(card.dataset.id, direction), });
In React:
const list = useSortable<HTMLUListElement>({ onReorder: (from, to) => setItems((x) => arrayMove(x, from, to)), });

import { carousel, dialog, drawer, pullToRefresh } from "@weber-development/lagrangian-pro";
pullToRefresh(scroller, { onRefresh: () => reload() }); carousel(viewport, { align: "center", label: "Photos" });
const menu = drawer(nav, { side: "left", backdrop: shade }); menuButton.onclick = () => menu.toggle();
const confirm = dialog(box, { backdrop: shade }); deleteButton.onclick = () => confirm.show();
In React:
const menu = useDrawer({ side: "right" }); return <nav ref={menu.ref}>…</nav>;

import { fall, indicator, toasts } from "@weber-development/lagrangian-pro";
const stack = toasts(corner, { edge: "bottom", max: 4 }); saveButton.onclick = () => stack.show("Saved");
indicator(tabs, bar, { itemSelector: "button", onSelect: (i) => showPanel(i) });
const effect = fall(section); effect.start(); effect.explode({ x: 400, y: 600 }); await effect.restore();

